WEBVTT

00:00:01.440 --> 00:00:04.360
<i>The mythical feint born 
from a coincidence.</i>

00:00:04.360 --> 00:00:06.650
<i>I tried again and again,</i>

00:00:06.650 --> 00:00:08.820
<i>but wasn't able to 
pull it off in the match.</i>

00:00:08.820 --> 00:00:12.450
<i>Still, our Enoshima Soccer Club</i>

00:00:12.450 --> 00:00:14.890
<i>continued to win in the qualifiers.</i>

00:00:15.360 --> 00:00:19.050
<i>Meanwhile, I met up with 
someone I once seriously injured,</i>

00:00:19.050 --> 00:00:22.120
<i>my childhood friend, Koichi Hibino.</i>

00:00:22.120 --> 00:00:26.460
<i>Hibino continued to play soccer 
on his unrecovered knee.</i>

00:00:26.980 --> 00:00:30.000
<i>In the end, we never quite connected.</i>

00:02:00.760 --> 00:02:06.020
<b>Strong Opponent?! Tsujido</b>

00:02:07.200 --> 00:02:08.930
The time has finally come!

00:02:08.930 --> 00:02:11.010
The final regional match in 
the Kanagawa prefecturals,

00:02:11.010 --> 00:02:13.590
Enoshima High versus Tsujido!

00:02:13.590 --> 00:02:15.240
Up until now, our Enoshima Soccer Club

00:02:15.240 --> 00:02:17.680
has won three matches against other schools

00:02:17.680 --> 00:02:18.950
with incredible strength.

00:02:18.950 --> 00:02:21.050
If they can defeat Tsujido,

00:02:18.950 --> 00:02:24.870
<b>Enoshima Broadcast Club</b>

00:02:21.050 --> 00:02:23.590
they will be entered into 
the Kanagawa qualifier:

00:02:23.590 --> 00:02:24.870
the final tournament.

00:02:24.870 --> 00:02:26.610
Shut up! Go home.

00:02:26.610 --> 00:02:28.020
You're annoying!

00:02:28.830 --> 00:02:31.260
What a cheering squad, huh, Kota?

00:02:28.830 --> 00:02:35.210
<b>Fight!</b>

00:02:28.830 --> 00:02:35.210
Show 'em!

00:02:31.260 --> 00:02:33.620
Man, I really want to play!

00:02:33.620 --> 00:02:35.210
You'll have your chance.

00:02:35.730 --> 00:02:38.630
I have a feeling that today's 
match will be a little different.

00:02:40.520 --> 00:02:44.090
Right. They just don't
 look like a team that

00:02:44.090 --> 00:02:45.590
could've defeated the 
powerful All Japan team.

00:02:45.590 --> 00:02:48.100
They're late, and they 
aren't even warming up.

00:02:48.100 --> 00:02:49.680
Don't underestimate them.

00:02:50.450 --> 00:02:52.670
In the past matches,
when the whistle blew

00:02:52.670 --> 00:02:55.800
they got it together and played 
unbelievably well together.

00:02:55.800 --> 00:02:59.070
I think they've already warmed up.

00:02:59.350 --> 00:03:03.070
It's evident.
 Look, their shirts are sweaty.

00:03:05.350 --> 00:03:08.020
They look like a gang or something.

00:03:08.020 --> 00:03:09.540
Indeed.

00:03:09.540 --> 00:03:10.810
Coach!

00:03:10.810 --> 00:03:15.550
I've strategized all I could 
strategize this last week.

00:03:15.550 --> 00:03:17.170
Let's be confident and play.

00:03:17.170 --> 00:03:18.200
Yeah!

00:03:22.060 --> 00:03:24.600
First, the starters for Enoshima High...

00:03:24.600 --> 00:03:27.850
the strong goal keeper, Reo Kurebayashi!

00:03:28.620 --> 00:03:29.850
Reo-kun!

00:03:30.280 --> 00:03:31.680
Thanks!

00:03:35.190 --> 00:03:38.780
The two-back system we've seen 
in past matches is here again.

00:03:39.120 --> 00:03:41.700
First, the physically strong Go Kaiouji.

00:03:42.500 --> 00:03:43.680
Kaiouji!

00:03:43.680 --> 00:03:45.050
We're with you!

00:03:45.430 --> 00:03:46.740
Just the guys?

00:03:47.190 --> 00:03:50.380
The sniper with the cruel 
smile, Akito Horikawa.

00:03:52.200 --> 00:03:53.390
Horikawa's creepy!

00:03:53.390 --> 00:03:55.710
Those girls... I'll kill you.

00:03:56.190 --> 00:03:59.730
The defensive midfielder with 
amazing physical fitness,

00:03:59.730 --> 00:04:01.330
in the center, Ryoma Oda.

00:04:01.330 --> 00:04:02.720
Oda-san!

00:04:03.150 --> 00:04:05.380
On the left side, the 
captain, Yuji Sawamura.

00:04:05.380 --> 00:04:06.680
Sawamura-san!

00:04:06.680 --> 00:04:10.510
On the right side, today 
we have the tall Sakamoto.

00:04:11.110 --> 00:04:12.180
Who's that?

00:04:12.800 --> 00:04:16.080
The offensive midfielders, 
of course, are these two.

00:04:16.080 --> 00:04:17.780
They can protect and attack,

00:04:17.780 --> 00:04:20.400
the stable Makoto Hyodo and 
the pride of the Enoshima,

00:04:20.400 --> 00:04:23.800
the fantasista, the magician 
on the second line,

00:04:23.800 --> 00:04:25.380
number 10, Ryuichi Araki!

00:04:25.380 --> 00:04:26.620
Mako-kun!

00:04:26.620 --> 00:04:29.660
Araki-kun! Lose some weight!

00:04:29.660 --> 00:04:31.870
I have lost quite a bit!

00:04:32.240 --> 00:04:34.330
And now, the forwards...

00:04:34.330 --> 00:04:37.040
On the right side, the 
technician, Kaoru Matoba.

00:04:37.040 --> 00:04:39.070
Kaoru-kun!

00:04:39.720 --> 00:04:42.100
Kaoru-kun! You're cute!

00:04:42.100 --> 00:04:44.220
Don't call me cute.

00:04:44.220 --> 00:04:47.050
The center forward, with three goals,

00:04:47.050 --> 00:04:49.010
the ace striker, Junpei Hino.

00:04:49.010 --> 00:04:51.590
And on the left, the huge forward,

00:04:51.590 --> 00:04:53.300
Michiro Takase.

00:04:54.140 --> 00:04:56.040
Enoshima Tower!

00:04:57.410 --> 00:05:01.120
I'll present the lineup 
for the opposing Tsujido.

00:05:01.120 --> 00:05:03.610
Goal keeper, number 1, Mikio Onizuka.

00:05:03.920 --> 00:05:05.820
The defenders are 
in a four-back layout.

00:05:05.820 --> 00:05:08.070
The right side is number 4,
 Kei Ishikawa.

00:05:08.070 --> 00:05:10.570
The center-backs are 
number 2, Tooru Akagi

00:05:10.570 --> 00:05:12.420
and number 3, Sho Sugama.

00:05:12.420 --> 00:05:14.580
The left side is number 5, Kenta Honda.

00:05:15.060 --> 00:05:18.080
The defensive midfielders, 
number 6, Kinichi Fuwa,

00:05:18.080 --> 00:05:19.920
and number 8, Kazuo Kumada.

00:05:20.630 --> 00:05:22.920
Three offensive midfielders, 
from the right,

00:05:22.920 --> 00:05:25.800
number 11, Shintaro Seta.

00:05:25.800 --> 00:05:28.590
Below the top, number 10, Tae-Seung Kim.

00:05:28.590 --> 00:05:30.850
On the left, Nobuaki Shindo, number 7.

00:05:31.370 --> 00:05:33.150
The forward is number 9,

00:05:33.150 --> 00:05:35.170
Kyosuke Hasegawa, 
in a one-top formation.

00:05:35.170 --> 00:05:38.600
The Tsujido Eleven look like 
they're ready for a figh—

00:05:38.600 --> 00:05:40.840
I mean, they look physically strong!

00:05:40.840 --> 00:05:43.880
Hey, Sho! Back up. I'll kill you.

00:05:43.880 --> 00:05:45.860
Shut up, Kim. I know.

00:05:45.860 --> 00:05:47.910
Hey, if it isn't Jun Hino.

00:05:47.910 --> 00:05:48.860
Huh?

00:05:48.860 --> 00:05:51.830
Left the group and went back to soccer?

00:05:51.830 --> 00:05:53.350
Oh, it's Fuwa.

00:05:53.350 --> 00:05:55.990
What's someone like you doing here?

00:05:55.990 --> 00:06:00.040
Keep talking. I'll never 
let you get your job done.

00:06:01.480 --> 00:06:03.530
Let it go, Junpei. 
It's kickoff time.

00:06:06.160 --> 00:06:09.300
It's Enoshima's ball for 
the first half kickoff.

00:06:10.460 --> 00:06:11.990
Hino passes the ball 
to Hyodo right away,

00:06:11.990 --> 00:06:14.640
and leaves the center 
circle aggressively.

00:06:15.070 --> 00:06:18.410
Here come Tsujido's Fuwa 
and Kumada yelling!

00:06:18.410 --> 00:06:19.650
What energy!

00:06:19.650 --> 00:06:20.850
What's this?

00:06:20.850 --> 00:06:22.030
I'm counting on you.

00:06:23.830 --> 00:06:24.730
Araki!

00:06:24.730 --> 00:06:26.230
I'll take that.

00:06:28.860 --> 00:06:30.070
He's lost the ball!

00:06:32.190 --> 00:06:33.980
Isn't that a foul?

00:06:33.980 --> 00:06:36.800
No. He approached his 
mark from a blind spot

00:06:36.800 --> 00:06:38.750
and cleanly went for the ball.

00:06:39.030 --> 00:06:40.210
All right.

00:06:40.210 --> 00:06:41.720
Here comes Shindo up the side.

00:06:41.720 --> 00:06:43.280
He's bringing it in with a dribble.

00:06:43.280 --> 00:06:44.340
I won't let you!

00:06:45.240 --> 00:06:46.800
Watch out, Sakamoto!

00:06:47.340 --> 00:06:48.010
Huh?

00:06:49.930 --> 00:06:52.970
Tsujido's Shindo miskicks.

00:06:52.970 --> 00:06:56.710
He's hit Sakamoto with the 
ball and created a throw-in.

00:07:00.390 --> 00:07:01.440
What's this?

00:07:01.440 --> 00:07:03.860
Kim comes upfield for the throw-in.

00:07:03.860 --> 00:07:06.280
What could be behind this excitement?

00:07:08.030 --> 00:07:09.810
The center-backs started running.

00:07:09.810 --> 00:07:10.900
It's started.

00:07:10.900 --> 00:07:12.990
Takase-kun, cover the goal!

00:07:12.990 --> 00:07:14.180
Okay!

00:07:15.260 --> 00:07:16.960
What could these movements be?

00:07:16.960 --> 00:07:18.800
Hasegawa leaves his forward position,

00:07:18.800 --> 00:07:21.980
and two tall center-backs are 
sprinting at full speed

00:07:21.980 --> 00:07:23.810
towards the Enoshima goal.

00:07:23.810 --> 00:07:26.600
What could this be about? 
I have no idea!

00:07:30.830 --> 00:07:32.470
Number 10, Tae-Seung Kim,

00:07:32.470 --> 00:07:34.370
approaches and throws...

00:07:37.570 --> 00:07:39.480
There it goes. What?!

00:07:40.330 --> 00:07:41.890
It really went.

00:07:43.380 --> 00:07:45.290
What is this throw-in?

00:07:45.290 --> 00:07:47.820
The ball traveled over 30 meters!

00:07:48.360 --> 00:07:50.280
It's mine!

00:07:52.240 --> 00:07:53.320
Takase clears it!

00:07:53.320 --> 00:07:54.700
Wait, the ball's still in play.

00:07:56.410 --> 00:07:58.120
No way. No way. No way!

00:07:58.740 --> 00:08:00.120
Nice defense by Horikawa.

00:08:00.120 --> 00:08:01.580
Enoshima is saved.

00:08:01.580 --> 00:08:02.590
Shit!

00:08:02.590 --> 00:08:03.540
So close!

00:08:04.750 --> 00:08:08.710
Even so, that throw-in 
was like a laser beam.

00:08:09.080 --> 00:08:10.370
That was close.

00:08:10.370 --> 00:08:13.890
We all saw it in the video, 
but I couldn't believe it.

00:08:19.400 --> 00:08:22.230
<i>Looks like you did your research,</i>

00:08:22.230 --> 00:08:25.770
<i>but our truly frightening stuff 
is still to come, Iwaki.</i>

00:08:26.320 --> 00:08:27.940
Kim's corner kick!

00:08:27.940 --> 00:08:29.130
All right!

00:08:29.130 --> 00:08:30.130
Hasegawa jumps!

00:08:30.130 --> 00:08:31.200
You're easy.

00:08:31.200 --> 00:08:34.500
However, the goal keeper, Kurebayashi, 
securely catches it.

00:08:34.500 --> 00:08:36.770
Show us a comeback, Enoshima Eleven.

00:08:36.770 --> 00:08:38.280
Fly!

00:08:40.090 --> 00:08:41.450
Got it.

00:08:41.450 --> 00:08:42.890
Araki-san!

00:08:42.890 --> 00:08:44.160
It's Araki!

00:08:44.160 --> 00:08:46.010
Will it be a dribble penetration 
or a through pass?

00:08:46.010 --> 00:08:47.170
When this man has the ball,

00:08:47.170 --> 00:08:49.130
you get a feeling something's 
going to happen.

00:08:49.130 --> 00:08:50.590
Let's stop him!

00:08:50.590 --> 00:08:52.620
Fore-check, Shindo!

00:08:57.350 --> 00:08:58.930
You're persistent.

00:09:00.140 --> 00:09:01.730
Come at me!

00:09:02.340 --> 00:09:04.560
<i>They've got an unexpectedly 
organized defense.</i>

00:09:06.230 --> 00:09:07.410
I'm counting on you!

00:09:07.410 --> 00:09:08.230
Yeah!

00:09:08.230 --> 00:09:10.510
What happened, Araki-san?

00:09:10.510 --> 00:09:13.610
Show us your god-like feints!

00:09:13.610 --> 00:09:17.700
For a feint to work he needs 
either a one-on-one or speed,

00:09:18.180 --> 00:09:21.530
but Araki-san has at least 
two defenders marking him

00:09:21.530 --> 00:09:23.660
and one is in his blind spot 
waiting for an opportunity.

00:09:23.660 --> 00:09:27.880
Even Araki-san won't be able to 
easily penetrate with a dribble.

00:09:28.120 --> 00:09:31.370
But they have the same 
11 players, right?

00:09:31.370 --> 00:09:34.400
If they're putting two or 
three players on Araki,

00:09:34.400 --> 00:09:36.900
then they're missing players 
elsewhere, right?

00:09:36.900 --> 00:09:37.840
That's true.

00:09:38.370 --> 00:09:40.490
That could be why the Tsujido defenders

00:09:40.490 --> 00:09:41.990
are gathered in the center,

00:09:41.990 --> 00:09:43.560
leaving the sides wide open.

00:09:43.830 --> 00:09:45.410
Then that's where we should aim

00:09:45.410 --> 00:09:47.270
and go for a sideline penetration!

00:09:47.570 --> 00:09:48.980
Go up the sides!

00:09:49.340 --> 00:09:50.400
All right!

00:09:50.400 --> 00:09:52.940
Sawamura-san and Sakamoto-san 
are running up the sides.

00:09:52.940 --> 00:09:54.740
Matoba is going to
 the sideline as well.

00:09:54.740 --> 00:09:58.200
With Oda-san's long feed, 
there might be a chance!

00:09:58.630 --> 00:09:59.660
That's strange.

00:09:59.660 --> 00:10:00.560
Huh?

00:10:00.560 --> 00:10:05.040
Indeed. I didn't notice in 
the last Tsujido match,

00:10:05.040 --> 00:10:08.060
but now that I think about it, 
the opponent at the time,

00:10:08.060 --> 00:10:11.130
All Japan High, didn't attempt 
a side penetration...

00:10:11.620 --> 00:10:14.090
Could the open sides be a trap?

00:10:14.090 --> 00:10:14.950
A trap?

00:10:14.950 --> 00:10:15.800
This is bad!

00:10:15.800 --> 00:10:17.630
Go!

00:10:17.630 --> 00:10:19.170
The sides are no good!

00:10:19.170 --> 00:10:19.740
What?

00:10:19.740 --> 00:10:20.930
There it is!

00:10:20.930 --> 00:10:23.260
Oda's pin point long feed.

00:10:23.260 --> 00:10:25.310
It's a straight shot to Matoba!

00:10:25.310 --> 00:10:27.020
This is their chance!

00:10:27.450 --> 00:10:28.440
Okay.

00:10:32.300 --> 00:10:33.910
We're not letting you through!

00:10:34.860 --> 00:10:35.780
Good.

00:10:36.150 --> 00:10:38.490
If we can stop them in the middle 
of their breakthrough...

00:10:38.490 --> 00:10:39.510
Takase!

00:10:40.060 --> 00:10:42.460
Tsujido's Kim intercepts!

00:10:42.460 --> 00:10:43.200
All right!

00:10:43.200 --> 00:10:44.160
Here we go!

00:10:44.700 --> 00:10:47.530
It looked like an opportunity. 
Tsujido's forward, Hasegawa,

00:10:47.530 --> 00:10:49.370
and midfielder, 
Seta, break into a run.

00:10:50.790 --> 00:10:53.870
They've broken into the penalty area.

00:10:53.870 --> 00:10:55.500
Seems a little over-eager.

00:10:55.500 --> 00:10:56.760
Take it back!

00:11:00.020 --> 00:11:01.890
Kim miskicks and it's a side out.

00:11:02.470 --> 00:11:04.850
<i>Not with Tsujido still 
in the penalty area!</i>

00:11:05.650 --> 00:11:07.180
Go!

00:11:08.370 --> 00:11:09.860
Here it is again!

00:11:09.860 --> 00:11:12.270
Number 10, Kim's laser beam throw!

00:11:12.860 --> 00:11:15.440
Hasegawa received it 
in the penalty area!

00:11:15.440 --> 00:11:17.190
He's obviously offsides!

00:11:17.740 --> 00:11:19.400
There's no flag?

00:11:19.400 --> 00:11:21.170
Horikawa is trying to chase it down.

00:11:21.170 --> 00:11:23.370
Goal keeper Kurebayashi 
jumps out as well!

00:11:27.770 --> 00:11:30.250
They've scored a goal!

00:11:33.280 --> 00:11:35.670
Wasn't that offsides?

00:11:35.670 --> 00:11:37.780
I see. So that's what it was!

00:11:37.780 --> 00:11:39.220
It was not offsides.

00:11:39.220 --> 00:11:40.380
That shot was good.

00:11:40.380 --> 00:11:42.890
It's 1-0 at 15 minutes into the first half.

00:11:42.890 --> 00:11:45.350
The first goal is scored by Tsujido!

00:11:45.350 --> 00:11:47.670
That had to be offsides, right?

00:11:47.670 --> 00:11:48.530
Kota...

00:11:48.530 --> 00:11:49.580
I mean,

00:11:49.580 --> 00:11:52.140
when that Kim guy threw in the ball,

00:11:52.140 --> 00:11:53.570
number 11 and number 9

00:11:53.570 --> 00:11:56.070
were past the defenders' last line.

00:11:56.390 --> 00:11:58.400
The defensive line doesn't matter.

00:11:58.400 --> 00:11:59.030
Why not?

00:11:59.590 --> 00:12:03.230
Offside rules don't apply to throw-ins.

00:12:03.690 --> 00:12:05.740
I didn't know that. Really?

00:12:06.170 --> 00:12:08.890
Kaiouji and the others 
should have already known

00:12:08.890 --> 00:12:11.210
that you can't be 
offsides on a throw-in,

00:12:11.670 --> 00:12:14.740
but even if you imagined that 
a throw-in from that position

00:12:14.740 --> 00:12:16.780
could reach the penalty 
area like a free kick,

00:12:16.780 --> 00:12:20.450
their bodies just didn't 
respond in time.

00:12:20.450 --> 00:12:22.020
That was my mistake.

00:12:22.020 --> 00:12:22.930
Coach Iwaki.

00:12:23.250 --> 00:12:25.540
Predicting the opponent's strategy

00:12:25.540 --> 00:12:28.670
and reacting immediately 
is the coach's job.

00:12:31.530 --> 00:12:34.500
Don't aim for the opponent's 
sidelines carelessly.

00:12:34.500 --> 00:12:38.330
Also, even if the forward, 
number 9 is offsides,

00:12:38.330 --> 00:12:40.040
Kaiouji, stick to him like glue.

00:12:40.040 --> 00:12:40.820
All right.

00:12:41.550 --> 00:12:42.280
Araki!

00:12:42.280 --> 00:12:45.490
Our ball control is far better,

00:12:45.490 --> 00:12:47.710
but we never know when 
their laser beam is coming,

00:12:47.710 --> 00:12:49.200
so we can't let our guard down.

00:12:53.950 --> 00:12:56.330
They have a considerable defense.

00:12:56.770 --> 00:12:59.300
The four defenders have 
left the sides open

00:12:59.300 --> 00:13:01.300
and concentrated in the middle,

00:13:01.740 --> 00:13:05.010
so Araki can't find a 
gap for a through pass.

00:13:05.360 --> 00:13:07.970
Meanwhile, the wide open 
sidelines might be a trap.

00:13:09.390 --> 00:13:11.170
Triple teaming?

00:13:11.170 --> 00:13:12.050
Araki!

00:13:12.390 --> 00:13:13.390
Take it!

00:13:14.610 --> 00:13:15.520
Fuwa!

00:13:16.300 --> 00:13:19.610
I told you I wasn't going to 
let you do your job, Jun Hino.

00:13:20.970 --> 00:13:22.590
You!

00:13:26.370 --> 00:13:28.870
That was a dangerous tackle!

00:13:30.130 --> 00:13:32.020
The ref raises a card!

00:13:32.020 --> 00:13:35.450
Number 9, Junpei Hino, 
receives a yellow card.

00:13:35.450 --> 00:13:37.440
Hey, Junpei, don't get hot-headed.

00:13:37.440 --> 00:13:39.420
Shit! He's pissing me off!

00:13:40.750 --> 00:13:43.630
Don't get mad so easily and foul me.

00:13:44.030 --> 00:13:45.310
Why you...

00:13:45.310 --> 00:13:46.590
Junpei, stop it!

00:13:49.610 --> 00:13:51.500
<i>That number 10 again.</i>

00:13:52.200 --> 00:13:54.520
<i>Just in case, I'll mark the forward.</i>

00:13:57.950 --> 00:14:00.610
Shoot! Kaiouji-kun, bring up the line!

00:14:00.610 --> 00:14:01.570
Oh, no!

00:14:02.110 --> 00:14:03.780
Kim swiftly free kicks!

00:14:04.300 --> 00:14:06.870
He's aiming for the space 
between Kaiouji,

00:14:06.870 --> 00:14:08.210
marking the forward Hasegawa,

00:14:08.210 --> 00:14:10.490
and Oda, who was upfield for the attack.

00:14:11.450 --> 00:14:13.640
Shit, shit, shit, shit!

00:14:13.640 --> 00:14:15.890
Horikawa sprints back on defense,

00:14:15.890 --> 00:14:18.690
but Seta is one step ahead of him.

00:14:18.690 --> 00:14:20.340
Hasegawa is signaling for the ball,

00:14:20.340 --> 00:14:22.290
but Kaiouji is marking him.

00:14:22.290 --> 00:14:24.760
Will Seta go for it?

00:14:24.760 --> 00:14:25.960
Come at me.

00:14:27.880 --> 00:14:29.220
What? A pass to the side?

00:14:31.000 --> 00:14:35.350
What's this? The center-back, 
Sugama, overlaps!

00:14:38.720 --> 00:14:40.270
It's mine!

00:14:43.130 --> 00:14:44.890
Kurebayashi gets a touch.

00:14:44.890 --> 00:14:46.820
Is it a goal? Is it safe?

00:14:53.650 --> 00:14:57.500
Goal!

00:15:01.650 --> 00:15:03.610
<b><i>Tsujido

00:15:02.470 --> 00:15:04.070
It's 2-0!

00:15:04.070 --> 00:15:05.990
Too cautious of Kim's long throw,

00:15:05.990 --> 00:15:08.440
Enoshima High's defense had holes,

00:15:08.440 --> 00:15:11.260
which Tsujido spectacularly aimed for!

00:15:13.530 --> 00:15:14.880
They're strong.

00:15:14.880 --> 00:15:15.890
Huh?

00:15:17.910 --> 00:15:21.020
Tsujido is really strong.

00:15:22.550 --> 00:15:23.730
Kakeru?

00:15:26.710 --> 00:15:28.330
<i>I want to get into this match.</i>

00:15:29.210 --> 00:15:32.950
<i>Brother, I want to fight, too.</i>

00:15:48.010 --> 00:15:50.170
<i>Our team is in trouble, but...</i>

00:15:51.180 --> 00:15:53.140
<i>I can't help feeling excited.</i>

00:15:54.130 --> 00:15:56.100
<i>It seems like my brother's 
heart is saying,</i>

00:15:57.060 --> 00:16:00.060
<i>"I want to play against a 
strong team like this."</i>

00:16:07.650 --> 00:16:09.180
Kakeru.

00:16:09.670 --> 00:16:11.490
Wh-What is it, Seven?

00:16:16.830 --> 00:16:19.660
Do you remember, Kakeru?

00:16:20.130 --> 00:16:21.080
What?

00:16:22.130 --> 00:16:24.400
When the opponent scores a goal,

00:16:24.400 --> 00:16:26.620
and it feels like the game is over,

00:16:26.620 --> 00:16:27.540
Suguru-san would...

00:16:31.740 --> 00:16:34.810
It's 2-0. We're in a bind, Kakeru.

00:16:34.810 --> 00:16:35.720
Yeah.

00:16:35.720 --> 00:16:38.850
Idiots! It's only just starting.

00:16:38.850 --> 00:16:40.780
Things are only just starting 
to get interesting.

00:16:44.400 --> 00:16:48.430
He'd say that, and look so excited.

00:16:48.430 --> 00:16:52.030
Then, he'd always score a goal.

00:16:52.970 --> 00:16:54.670
What's going on, Seven?

00:16:54.670 --> 00:16:56.560
Why are you bringing this up?

00:16:58.450 --> 00:17:00.410
The game is only just starting, right?

00:17:01.860 --> 00:17:03.620
Yeah. Of course!

00:17:09.860 --> 00:17:11.010
Araki!

00:17:11.330 --> 00:17:12.360
Hino!

00:17:13.150 --> 00:17:15.300
There it is! Araki's through pass!

00:17:15.300 --> 00:17:16.720
It's going to Hino...

00:17:20.450 --> 00:17:23.310
No! He's brought down by Fuwa's tackle.

00:17:23.310 --> 00:17:24.510
Is there a foul?

00:17:24.510 --> 00:17:26.100
No, the ref lets it go.

00:17:27.510 --> 00:17:29.570
That's how you do a tackle.

00:17:29.960 --> 00:17:32.050
You...

00:17:32.050 --> 00:17:33.530
Fuwa, you son of a bitch!

00:17:33.530 --> 00:17:34.610
Cut it out, Hino!

00:17:37.950 --> 00:17:39.640
That's no good.

00:17:39.640 --> 00:17:41.620
Enoshima's forward, Junpei Hino,

00:17:41.620 --> 00:17:45.580
was riled up by Tsujido's 
Fuwa, and grabbed him!

00:17:46.280 --> 00:17:50.450
That's his second yellow card 
this game, which means...

00:17:50.450 --> 00:17:51.730
You're out.

00:17:51.730 --> 00:17:53.590
No, but this guy...

00:17:53.590 --> 00:17:54.840
Junpei!

00:17:56.660 --> 00:17:58.390
He's been removed!

00:17:58.390 --> 00:18:01.710
At two goals behind, with the 
loss of their ace striker,

00:18:01.710 --> 00:18:06.230
and left with only 10 players, 
Enoshima's in a bind!

00:18:09.180 --> 00:18:11.440
That's the end of the first half.

00:18:12.260 --> 00:18:14.400
It's 2-0, and only 10 players 
in the second half.

00:18:14.400 --> 00:18:17.360
This is a disastrous 
situation for Enoshima.

00:18:21.880 --> 00:18:23.800
C-Coach Kondo...

00:18:23.800 --> 00:18:25.250
You idiot!

00:18:29.270 --> 00:18:31.960
If you just kept yourself from 
losing your temper so easily,

00:18:31.960 --> 00:18:33.300
even when you were on SC,

00:18:33.300 --> 00:18:35.880
you would have undoubtedly been 
a regular from your first year.

00:18:36.500 --> 00:18:39.320
B-But they were playing dirty!

00:18:39.320 --> 00:18:41.930
Tsujido's plays were dirty?

00:18:41.930 --> 00:18:44.180
Take a look at the scorebook.

00:18:48.010 --> 00:18:50.460
In the first half, including the 
yellow card you just received,

00:18:50.460 --> 00:18:52.370
we had five fouls.

00:18:52.370 --> 00:18:56.740
Tsujido, however, hasn't 
been called for a foul once!

00:19:01.180 --> 00:19:03.330
I'm sorry.

00:19:03.870 --> 00:19:06.370
They may come off as somewhat rude,

00:19:06.370 --> 00:19:09.840
but Tsujido's soccer is clean, organized,

00:19:09.840 --> 00:19:12.380
and above all else, truly strong!

00:19:14.540 --> 00:19:16.330
Acknowledge that and,
 in the second half,

00:19:16.330 --> 00:19:18.660
fight as a challenger!

00:19:18.660 --> 00:19:19.400
All right?

00:19:19.400 --> 00:19:20.050
Yes!

00:19:21.030 --> 00:19:22.400
Coach Iwaki?

00:19:23.880 --> 00:19:26.750
Mishima-san, I'll be right back,

00:19:26.750 --> 00:19:29.010
so take care of distributing water.

00:19:29.010 --> 00:19:30.430
O-Okay.

00:19:40.970 --> 00:19:43.810
I've got to do something... something...

00:19:44.480 --> 00:19:45.680
This is happening because...

00:19:45.680 --> 00:19:47.370
It's your fault!

00:19:49.020 --> 00:19:50.160
Uryu.

00:19:50.160 --> 00:19:52.370
That's what you were thinking, right?

00:19:53.960 --> 00:19:56.160
You've always been like that.

00:19:56.590 --> 00:19:59.970
You take everything on and 
try to do it yourself.

00:19:59.970 --> 00:20:01.800
Just like in that match, 10 years ago.

00:20:03.810 --> 00:20:06.310
I'll tell you one thing, Teppei.

00:20:07.770 --> 00:20:10.270
If you think it's all your fault,

00:20:10.270 --> 00:20:12.230
it's because you don't 
trust your teammates.

00:20:13.780 --> 00:20:16.650
Don't let me down in the second half.

00:20:24.580 --> 00:20:25.570
Coach!

00:20:26.170 --> 00:20:27.820
Among the reserve players,

00:20:27.820 --> 00:20:30.010
if there's anyone who 
really wants to play,

00:20:30.010 --> 00:20:31.040
raise your hand.

00:20:34.240 --> 00:20:34.920
Yes!

00:20:37.130 --> 00:20:38.250
Me, too!

00:20:40.070 --> 00:20:42.180
Oh, Ri-kun, too?

00:20:42.180 --> 00:20:43.500
Please use me.

00:20:43.500 --> 00:20:46.350
I won't let them have another goal.

00:20:47.250 --> 00:20:48.540
I see.

00:20:48.540 --> 00:20:51.810
Then, as of the second half,
 you're in for Kurebayashi-kun.

00:20:52.690 --> 00:20:53.480
Yes!

00:20:54.040 --> 00:20:57.480
Kota-kun, Kakeru-kun, 
start warming up.

00:20:58.230 --> 00:21:00.670
You're in for the second half, as well.

00:21:03.050 --> 00:21:03.700
Yes!

00:21:04.140 --> 00:21:08.120
I'll be changing our system and 
strategy in the second half,

00:21:08.120 --> 00:21:11.330
but more important than anything 
is your fighting spirit.

00:21:11.810 --> 00:21:14.410
Change the flow of the game 
with your fighting spirit.

00:21:14.410 --> 00:21:15.770
I trust you guys.

00:21:15.770 --> 00:21:16.540
Yes!

00:21:22.860 --> 00:21:25.920
Did you wash your face and 
feel refreshed, Iwaki-kun?

00:21:27.060 --> 00:21:29.080
Uryu set me straight.

00:21:29.080 --> 00:21:29.850
Uryu did?

00:21:30.270 --> 00:21:33.180
Yes. He asked me if I was going to 
keep swinging at windmills.

00:21:33.780 --> 00:21:36.290
"If you blame yourself,

00:21:36.290 --> 00:21:38.500
it's because you don't 
trust your teammates."

00:21:38.500 --> 00:21:40.160
That really hit me.

00:21:41.970 --> 00:21:43.240
Iwaki-kun.

00:21:43.720 --> 00:21:45.860
Thanks to him, I remembered.

00:21:45.860 --> 00:21:49.240
I remembered the regret I had left 
behind in high school soccer.

00:21:50.850 --> 00:21:53.080
But it's all right now.

00:21:53.080 --> 00:21:54.750
We still have plenty of time.

00:21:55.380 --> 00:21:58.960
To start off with, let's have our 
wonderful teammates get to work.

00:21:59.600 --> 00:22:03.170
I plan to try my best to come up 
with something in the mean time.

00:22:03.480 --> 00:22:05.210
A strategy...

00:22:05.750 --> 00:22:07.630
that will take down my greatest rival.

00:22:09.240 --> 00:22:11.690
We're approaching the 
second half kickoff.

00:22:11.690 --> 00:22:14.280
Enoshima suffered the loss 
of their ace striker, Hino,

00:22:14.280 --> 00:22:16.240
and put in the forward 
who's had two goals so far,

00:22:16.240 --> 00:22:18.600
the first year, Kakeru Aizawa.

00:22:18.600 --> 00:22:21.110
On the left side, with 
the aggressive attack,

00:22:21.110 --> 00:22:22.520
also a first year, Kota Nakatsuka,

00:22:22.520 --> 00:22:26.200
and the goal keeper, Kurebayashi, 
who's allowed two goals this match,

00:22:26.200 --> 00:22:28.410
has been replaced by third year, Akitoshi Ri.

00:22:28.900 --> 00:22:30.180
Go get them!

00:22:30.180 --> 00:22:31.330
Comeback time!

00:22:31.770 --> 00:22:34.290
C'mon, Tsujido!

00:22:34.950 --> 00:22:36.970
<i>I've got to get forward somehow.</i>

00:22:36.970 --> 00:22:39.540
<i>Being two goals down, 
just defending won't...</i>

00:22:42.140 --> 00:22:44.090
Give me the ball! The ball!

00:22:44.090 --> 00:22:46.010
What's with this guy?!

00:22:48.920 --> 00:22:50.090
He's so persistent!

00:22:51.250 --> 00:22:53.560
<i>Instead of throwing in, 
he sent it to the middle?</i>

00:22:55.830 --> 00:22:57.020
Side change!

00:22:57.020 --> 00:22:58.980
The ball goes to Shindo on the left side.

00:22:59.440 --> 00:23:00.690
<i>I won't let you through here.</i>

00:23:02.590 --> 00:23:03.610
Shoot!

00:23:04.510 --> 00:23:06.660
They went for the throw-in again.

00:23:06.660 --> 00:23:08.070
Could this again be...

00:23:08.700 --> 00:23:10.030
I'll do it!

00:23:10.450 --> 00:23:12.630
Shit! Here it comes again.

00:23:12.630 --> 00:23:15.330
Kaiouji, leave number 9 to me.

00:23:15.330 --> 00:23:18.170
Keep an eye on the number 2, 
number 3 overlap.

00:23:18.170 --> 00:23:19.240
Got it.

00:23:21.360 --> 00:23:23.770
There it is! The laser beam throw!

00:23:23.770 --> 00:23:25.130
A distance of 40 meters

00:23:25.130 --> 00:23:27.880
covered instantly and 
heading for the goal.

00:23:28.990 --> 00:23:29.600
You're mi—

00:23:31.920 --> 00:23:33.300
It's Ri! He's high!

00:23:36.540 --> 00:23:38.300
Nice one, Ri-kun!

00:23:40.520 --> 00:23:42.870
The ball goes straight back 
onto Tsujido's side.

00:23:42.870 --> 00:23:44.230
The first chance in a 
while for Enoshima.

00:23:44.230 --> 00:23:45.900
All right. Let's go, Kakeru.

00:23:45.900 --> 00:23:47.440
I'll put it away!

00:23:47.440 --> 00:23:48.900
As if I'd let you!

00:24:03.110 --> 00:24:04.180
All right.

00:24:04.600 --> 00:24:06.150
In a harsh contest for a header,

00:24:06.150 --> 00:24:07.790
both players went flying head over heels.

00:24:07.790 --> 00:24:08.840
Are they all right?

00:24:08.840 --> 00:24:10.170
Kakeru!

00:24:10.170 --> 00:24:11.670
The ball is Tsujido's.

00:24:11.670 --> 00:24:13.530
Kim heads in with a dribble.

00:24:13.530 --> 00:24:15.170
They're pushing in! 
Enoshima's in a pinch.

00:24:15.170 --> 00:24:16.370
We won't let you into the area.

00:24:16.370 --> 00:24:17.390
No way, no way, no way.

00:24:17.390 --> 00:24:17.970
Kim!

00:24:18.410 --> 00:24:19.450
Shindo!

00:24:20.070 --> 00:24:21.140
Wh-What?

00:24:21.910 --> 00:24:24.480
Whoa! And the one who 
intercepted it was...

00:24:24.480 --> 00:24:25.230
Aizawa!

00:24:25.890 --> 00:24:27.270
Damn first year brat!

00:24:39.490 --> 00:24:40.640
Kakeru...

00:24:45.980 --> 00:25:15.450
<b>Next Episode
The Empty 3 Seconds</b>

00:24:46.990 --> 00:24:48.570
In the height of the 
match against Tsujido,

00:24:48.570 --> 00:24:50.570
a change occurred in Kakeru.

00:24:50.570 --> 00:24:52.370
While his opponents and 
teammates alike are thrown

00:24:52.370 --> 00:24:54.370
by plays that seem to 
belong to another person,

00:24:54.370 --> 00:24:56.000
Kakeru, caught up in the moment,

00:24:56.000 --> 00:24:59.010
presses in for the comeback goal.

00:24:59.010 --> 00:25:01.170
Not wanting to give anything 
to their opponents,

00:25:01.170 --> 00:25:02.960
both teams fight hard.

00:25:02.960 --> 00:25:05.650
Heading into the 
remaining time with a tie,

00:25:05.650 --> 00:25:08.940
Kakeru's mythical feint 
finally becomes reality.

00:25:09.480 --> 00:25:10.940
Next time on 
Knight in the Area,

00:25:10.940 --> 00:25:13.660
episode 16:
 "The Empty 3 Seconds."

00:25:13.660 --> 00:25:15.710
You finally did it, Kakeru!
